course: dictionary
lesson: 12330
title: A matching partner in another place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A counterpart is a person or thing that has the same job or place as another, but in a different group, country or situation. Think of two goalkeepers, one for your school and one for a school across the country. Each is the other's counterpart.
explain: «The Prime Minister met his French counterpart in Paris.» Both men lead their countries, so each has the same job as the other. The clue is that they are in different countries.
explain: Scientists use counterpart to compare matching things. «The human arm and the bird's wing are counterparts» means they do a similar job in different creatures, even though they look different. A quick check: ask yourself, is this matched with something that is in a different group?
fact: A counterpart is a person or thing with the same job or place as another, in a different group, country or situation.
fact: Counterpart is a noun, so you can write one counterpart or many counterparts.
fact: «The head teacher met her counterparts from other schools.» Each of them runs a different school.
fact: «A digital counterpart» is a version of something that exists on a computer or phone, such as an app version of a paper map.
fact: A good check is to swap in the words "matching one" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The Prime Minister met his French counterpart.» What is a counterpart here? | A plate of French food | A French car | A map of France | *The person with the same job in France
exercise: In science, the bird's wing is compared with which body part? | *The human arm | The tree's roots | The fish's tail | The bird's beak
exercise: Which word means a matching person or thing in another group or country? | Group | *Counterpart | Country | Teacher
test: «The head teacher met her counterparts from other schools.» Who are the counterparts? | *Other head teachers who do the same job | The school dinner ladies | The pupils at her school | The parents who wait at the gate
test: Which is the best example of a digital counterpart? | *An app version of a paper map on a phone | A map drawn by hand | A paper map kept in a drawer | A map of the moon
exam: Which sentence uses counterpart correctly? | *The mayor of our town met her counterpart from Spain | Counterpart is a loud noise in the kitchen | I counterpart my homework every night | The cat's counterpart is my favourite toy
